IMPORT prelude

-- Income Support Law 5741-1980 (Israel) -- shared nouns and three-valued helpers.
-- Hebrew: חוק הבטחת הכנסה, התשמ״א–1980.  Source: the unofficial Hebrew Wikisource text (see NOTES.md).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively).  This module holds DECLAREs and two tiny three-valued helpers; no section's rule lives here.
--
-- Numbering is a gloss of the Hebrew numbering: section 3א = `s 3A`, subsection (א) = (a), (ב1) = (b1), (2א) = (2A).
-- A decision function answers a MAYBE: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (only where the text says no in its own words) or NOTHING.

§ `Shared nouns`

-- The household the schedules classify by (Sch 2 and Sch 4 rows, Sch 3 rows, the "single person" and "spouses" definitions).
-- Every field is a fact the claimant can state; a field says in its name which definition of s 1 it carries.
-- A widow and an independent parent are two fields, not one: s 5(a)(3) sends an independent parent to rows (7) and (8) of the Second Schedule, and nothing in the text
-- does that for a widow who is not one (fork `second-schedule-widow-overlap-is-nothing`).  A positional record lists them in this order: spouse, children, widow, independent parent.
DECLARE Household HAS
    `the claimant has a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of children with the claimant` IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant is a widow` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is an independent parent` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The figures the Law leaves to the Institute's tables and to the Insurance Law.  They are inputs, never typed from memory.
-- הסכום הבסיסי (s 1), השכר הממוצע (s 1), הסכום הבסיסי לילד (Sch 2 note), נקודת קיצבה (s 1).
DECLARE Figures HAS
    `the basic amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the average wage` IS A NUMBER
    `the basic amount for a child` IS A NUMBER
    `the value of one pension point` IS A NUMBER

-- The body whose finding makes a person "not placeable in any work" under s 2(a)(1), and the situation each body can find about.
-- (המוסד האמור in s 2(a)(1)(a) is read as the institution, defined by the Supervision Law, in which the person is treated; fork `institution-of-treatment` in NOTES.md.)
DECLARE Determiner IS ONE OF
    `a drug-addiction diagnosis centre approved by the Minister, or the institution in which the person is treated`
    `a probation officer`
    `an alcoholics treatment centre under the supervision of the Ministry`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Placement situation` IS ONE OF
    `treated in an institution or in drug withdrawal under a court probation order`
    `under the supervision of a probation officer under the Arrests Law`
    `staying at an alcoholics treatment centre under the supervision of the Ministry`
    `none of these`

-- Whose rate of s 1 "basic amount" update applies.
DECLARE `Update class` IS ONE OF
    `a recipient of an Insurance Law pension named in s 1 "basic amount" (1)(a), who is also entitled under this Law`
    `anyone else paid a benefit under this Law`

§ `Three-valued helpers`

-- Helper, not a section: Kleene AND over MAYBE BOOLEAN.  A FALSE operand makes the result FALSE (that operand is the text's no);
-- two TRUE operands make it TRUE; anything else is NOTHING.  It never turns a NOTHING into a FALSE.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`helper both` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE AND b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Helper, not a section: Kleene OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN.  A TRUE operand makes the result TRUE; two FALSE operands make it FALSE;
-- anything else is NOTHING.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`helper either` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE AND b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Helper, not a section: a MAYBE BOOLEAN made from a plain BOOLEAN; TRUE is JUST TRUE, FALSE is NOTHING (never JUST FALSE).
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`helper true or not covered` MEANS
    IF a THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
